{
  "id": "V21",
  "title": "Strong-Wall WSWH stack and raised floor",
  "intent": "Line A: two WSWH18 panels stacked over two 9 ft stories. The 2nd-story panel uses Table 03 and is held down by the TSS rod; the 1st-story panel is checked as an allowable base moment (M_allow = V₀·H₁/12 with V₀ at P = 4,000 lb, f'c 2,500) against M_d = [V₁·H₁ + V₂·(H₁ + d_fl + H₂)]/12, and its anchors carry the stack moment. Line B: one panel on a raised wood floor (Table 02): shear check and anchor tension T only — the anchorage is by the RDP.",
  "covers": [
    "C-L-SW26 Table 03 (stacked 2nd story)",
    "Table 01 stack base (README §5)",
    "Table 02 raised floor",
    "Table 06-A anchors",
    "TSS rod"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Line A shears (1.0E): 2nd story F = 0.8 k → V₂ = 0.80 k on SW-1; 1st story V₁ = 0.8 + 1 = 1.80 k on SW-2. ASD: V₂ = 0.7 × 800 = 559.9999999999999 lb, V₁ = 0.7 × 1800 = 1260 lb. No gravity on the panels (P = 0 ≤ 2,000 / 4,000 lb limits)."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "2nd story (Table 03, WSWH18x9): V_allow = 1,095 lb → D/C = 559.9999999999999/1095 = 0.511."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Stack base (Table 01 at P = 4,000 lb, f'c 2,500): V₀ = 2,575 lb, H₁ = 105.25 in → M_allow = 2575 × 105.25/12 = 22584.90 lb-ft."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "M_d = [V₁·H₁ + V₂·(H₁ + d_fl + H₂)]/12 = [1260 × 105.25 + 559.9999999999999 × (105.25 + 12 + 105.25)]/12 = 21434.58 lb-ft → D/C = M_d/M_allow = 0.949. Available V₁ = (M_allow − V₂·(H₁ + d_fl + H₂)/12)·12/H₁ = 1391.15 lb ≥ 1260 → OK."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "2nd-story hold-down: T = 0.7·V₂·H₂/B = 0.7 × 0.80 × 105.25/12.5 = 4.715 k (B = concrete B, Table 05-C, tool note) ≤ TSS rod 36,800 lb → rod."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Stack base anchors: M(1.0) = (V₁·H₁ + V₂·(H₁ + d_fl + H₂))/12 = (1.80 × 105.25 + 0.80 × 222.5)/12 = 30.621 k·ft → T = 0.7 × 30.621 / (12.5/12) = 20.577 k = 20577 lb. Table 06-A, SDC D, E rows: STD 16,000 / 17,100 < T → HS 34100 lb, W = 52 in, d_e = 18 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Drift: 2nd story Δ = 0.44 × 800/1095 = 0.321 in; base Δ₁ = Δ₀·M(1.0)/M_allow = 0.45 × 30620.83/22584.90 = 0.610 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Line B raised floor (Table 02, WSWH18x9, joist ≤ 12\"): V_allow = 1,475 lb; V = 1.00 k → D/C = 700/1475 = 0.475. T = 0.7·V·H_e/B = 0.7 × 1.00 × 105.25/14.0 = 5.263 k (B raised = 14.0 in) — reported; anchorage by the RDP."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Line checks G1–G12 pass on both lines; the 2nd-story panel end forces are absorbed into the stack base moment (not delivered as wall-end loads)."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Story drift, Line A (each story has one panel; table drift, ASD seismic column scaled to the 1.0E share, step 7). Story drift Level 2: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.3215 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.3215 / 1.0 = 1.286 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-2 0.6101 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.6101 / 1.0 = 2.440 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → NG — over the limit (design pinned, so drift sizing does not change it; the line reports drift NG). The stack base carries the moment of both stories, so its Δ₁ (0.610 in) is larger than the 2nd-story panel Δ."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "Story drift, Line B: SW-3 Δ = 0.43 × 1000.00 / 1475 = 0.292 in (Table 02). Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-3 0.2915 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.2915 / 1.0 = 1.166 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK."
    }
  ],
